@startuml ForsaDrive_Sequence_DriverApplication

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor User
participant "Mobile App\n(Flutter)" as UI
participant "PHP API\n(/admin/)" as Backend
database "SQLite DB" as DB
participant "Notification\nService" as Notif
actor Admin

title Sequence Diagram: Driver Application and Admin Approval

== User Submits Driver Application ==
User -> UI: Tap "Become a Driver"\nin Settings
activate UI
UI --> User: Show requirements page\n(CIN, license, vehicle needed)
User -> UI: Tap "Apply"
UI --> User: Show application form

User -> UI: Fill in:\n- CIN number\n- License number\n- Years of experience\n- Vehicle make/model/year\n- Plate number / seats / A/C\n- Notes (optional)

User -> UI: Submit application

UI -> Backend: POST /profile/\n{action: "apply_driver", cin: ...,\nlicense: ..., vehicle: {...}}
activate Backend

Backend -> DB: SELECT * FROM driver_applications\nWHERE user_id = ? AND status = 'pending'
activate DB
DB --> Backend: No pending application found
deactivate DB

Backend -> DB: INSERT driver_applications\n(user_id, cin, license, experience,\nvehicle_make/model/year/plate/seats,\nstatus = 'pending')
activate DB
DB --> Backend: Application created
deactivate DB

Backend --> UI: 200 — {status: "pending"}
deactivate Backend
UI --> User: Show status screen\n"Application submitted.\nWaiting for admin review."
deactivate UI

== Admin Reviews Application ==
Admin -> UI: Open Admin Panel\n→ Drivers tab
activate UI
UI -> Backend: GET /admin/?tab=drivers
activate Backend
Backend -> DB: SELECT * FROM driver_applications\nORDER BY status='pending' DESC
activate DB
DB --> Backend: Return all applications
deactivate DB
Backend --> UI: Return applications list
deactivate Backend
UI --> Admin: Show applications\n(pending first, with full vehicle details)
deactivate UI

Admin -> UI: Click on application\n→ Review CIN, license, vehicle info
activate UI

alt Admin approves
    Admin -> UI: Click "Approve"
    UI --> Admin: Confirmation dialog
    Admin -> UI: Confirm

    UI -> Backend: POST /admin/\n{action: "approve_driver",\nuser_id: X}
    activate Backend

    Backend -> DB: UPDATE driver_applications\nSET status = 'approved'
    activate DB
    DB --> Backend: Updated
    deactivate DB

    Backend -> DB: UPDATE users SET is_driver = 1\nWHERE id = X
    activate DB
    DB --> Backend: Updated
    deactivate DB

    Backend -> DB: INSERT INTO driver_profiles\n(user_id, reliabilityScore=50, ...)
    activate DB
    DB --> Backend: Profile created
    deactivate DB

    Backend -> DB: INSERT INTO vehicles\n(make, model, year, plate, seats,\nhas_ac) FROM application data
    activate DB
    DB --> Backend: Vehicle created
    deactivate DB

    Backend -> Notif: Send push notification\nto user: "Application approved!\nYou can now publish rides."
    activate Notif
    Notif --> Backend: Sent
    deactivate Notif

    Backend --> UI: 200 — success
    deactivate Backend
    UI --> Admin: Show "Driver approved" toast
    deactivate UI

else Admin rejects
    Admin -> UI: Click "Reject"
    UI --> Admin: Reason input dialog
    Admin -> UI: Enter reason\n(e.g. "License unclear")

    UI -> Backend: POST /admin/\n{action: "reject_driver",\nuser_id: X, reason: "..."}
    activate Backend

    Backend -> DB: UPDATE driver_applications\nSET status = 'rejected',\nrejection_reason = "..."
    activate DB
    DB --> Backend: Updated
    deactivate DB

    Backend -> Notif: Send push notification\nto user: "Application rejected.\nReason: License unclear.\nYou may reapply."
    activate Notif
    Notif --> Backend: Sent
    deactivate Notif

    Backend --> UI: 200 — success
    deactivate Backend
    UI --> Admin: Show "Driver rejected" toast
    deactivate UI
end

== User Checks Status ==
User -> UI: Reopen Driver Application screen
activate UI
UI -> Backend: GET /profile/?action=my_driver_application
activate Backend
Backend -> DB: SELECT * FROM driver_applications\nWHERE user_id = ?
activate DB
DB --> Backend: Return latest application
deactivate DB
Backend --> UI: Return application with status
deactivate Backend
UI --> User: Show status card:\nApproved (green) or Rejected (red)\nwith reason and "Reapply" button
deactivate UI

@enduml
